# Skein third-party submodules (E1.I4 / bd skein-ca2).
#
# Policy: a dependency is a *submodule* when we build it from source and the
# upstream publishes no stable, hash-pinnable release tarball -- a git commit
# is itself a content hash, which is exactly the property the reproducible
# build needs. A dependency is a *vendored tarball* (native/sqlite/*.sha256)
# when upstream ships signed releases, and a *checked-in source copy*
# (native/sqlite/third_party/sqlite-vec-0.1.9, the SQLCipher amalgamation)
# when the source is small, rarely bumped, and we want it reviewable in-tree.
# All three appear in this repo on purpose; see native/llama/README.md §2 and
# docs/design/AMALGAMATION_POLICY.md.
#
# The commits these are pinned at live in `native/llama/PINNED_COMMIT`, not
# here: a gitlink alone says nothing about *why*, and `git submodule update
# --remote` will happily move it. `tools/ci/check-submodules.sh` fails the
# build if the gitlink or the checked-out commit disagrees with that file.
#
# Nothing here is built in-tree: native/llama/CMakeLists.txt consumes all
# three read-only via add_subdirectory / include paths, with every generated
# byte landing under inference-service/.cxx (skein-doq0's "never build in a
# dirty source tree").

[submodule "third_party/llama.cpp"]
	path = third_party/llama.cpp
	url = https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp

# Header-only. Supplies Vulkan-Hpp (<vulkan/vulkan.hpp>) and a current
# vulkan_core.h, neither of which the NDK r27c sysroot provides at a version
# ggml-vulkan can compile against. The Vulkan *loader* is still the NDK's.
[submodule "third_party/Vulkan-Headers"]
	path = third_party/Vulkan-Headers
	url = https://github.com/KhronosGroup/Vulkan-Headers

# Header-only. Required by ggml-vulkan's `find_package(SPIRV-Headers CONFIG
# REQUIRED)` and by its `#include <spirv/unified1/spirv.hpp>`.
[submodule "third_party/SPIRV-Headers"]
	path = third_party/SPIRV-Headers
	url = https://github.com/KhronosGroup/SPIRV-Headers
